{
  "dom_id": "question-117217",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14240607/assets/afc68dbb5c336cff31e75f5ed92dd853c8fc7ec43e8fa66539d27d83b9e2070f.png)\n\nA box with no lid and a square base has a manufacturing cost that depends on two materials. The material for the base costs $$3$ per square meter, and the material for the lateral faces costs $$5$ per square meter. The box must have a volume of $2\\,{m}^{3}.$\n\nWhat is the value of $x$ for the box that has the smallest production cost?",
